WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.040
Marvel keeps many secrets hidden behind the
Iron Curtain, and does just about anything

00:00:05.040 --> 00:00:06.720
it can to keep them from leaking.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.960
Duping actors with fake scripts so they don't
know what's true and what's completely made-up?

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.100
Been there, done that.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.260
Filming multiple different endings to obscure
the real conclusion?

00:00:15.260 --> 00:00:17.480
Yep, Marvel filmmakers have done that, too.

00:00:17.480 --> 00:00:21.320
These tactics may have worked to stop actors
from spilling the beans, but they apparently

00:00:21.330 --> 00:00:25.409
weren't aggressive enough to prevent others
from sharing sensitive information about Marvel's

00:00:25.409 --> 00:00:26.599
projects.

00:00:26.600 --> 00:00:29.540
And speaking of sensitive information: Spoilers
ahead.

00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:34.000
It appears that a good portion of Marvel's
plans post-Avengers: Endgame have leaked on

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:38.420
Twitter, both for Phase 4 of the films in
the Marvel Cinematic Universe and for a number

00:00:38.420 --> 00:00:41.720
of television shows coming to the Disney+
streaming service.

00:00:41.720 --> 00:00:46.620
And not just a few days ago or a week ahead
of Avengers: Endgame launching in theaters,

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:49.900
these purported leaks hit the web back in
December 2018.

00:00:49.900 --> 00:00:54.860
The details come from a semi-anonymous Twitter
user who goes by the name of Roger Wardell,

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:59.620
who began sharing what he described as "leaks"
for Avengers: Endgame at the end of last year.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:03.829
At the time, Wardell's tweets gained virtually
no traction, given that his profile offers

00:01:03.829 --> 00:01:08.680
virtually no identifying information other
than his name, which could be fake, and because

00:01:08.680 --> 00:01:11.430
there was no way to confirm his tweets as
factual.

00:01:11.430 --> 00:01:15.750
Looking at them now in retrospect, though,
the things he said about Endgame turned out

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:19.520
to be completely on-the-money... like, scarily
accurate.

00:01:20.360 --> 00:01:22.680
"Oh, I'm getting chills."

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:26.780
Wardell predicted that Thor would lose his
chiseled physique and, quote, "look a bit

00:01:26.780 --> 00:01:31.210
like his old friend Volstagg," that Agent
Carter actor James D'Arcy would make the jump

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:35.990
from Marvel TV to the MCU as Edwin Jarvis,
that Robert Redford would return as Secretary

00:01:35.990 --> 00:01:40.570
Alexander Pierce, that Scott Lang would mess
up "big time," and that Chris Evans would

00:01:40.570 --> 00:01:44.770
"play a completely different Steve Rogers"
in the film, seemingly referencing the choice

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.710
Steve made to stay in the past and live a
normal life with Peggy Carter before catching

00:01:48.710 --> 00:01:50.510
up to the present as an old man.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:56.380
He even nailed details like Thor decapitating
Thanos, Stan Lee making a cameo in the 1970s,

00:01:56.380 --> 00:02:00.420
and Brock Rumlow and Jack Rollins returning
to recreate the elevator scene from Captain

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:04.600
America: The Winter Soldier, including a hint
at Cap's now-famous line from the recreated

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:05.600
scene.

00:02:05.620 --> 00:02:06.960
You know the one.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:10.840
"Hail Hydra."

00:02:11.140 --> 00:02:15.960
By all accounts, Wardell was almost totally
right about what went down in Avengers: Endgame.

00:02:15.960 --> 00:02:20.680
This makes it far easier to believe what he
tweeted about Marvel's future is just as precise.

00:02:20.680 --> 00:02:22.420
Wardell claimed in one tweet:

00:02:22.420 --> 00:02:26.970
"While [Kevin] Feige has talked about films
based on Power Pack and Ms. Marvel, it's also

00:02:26.970 --> 00:02:31.730
being heavily discussed to have these as multiple
season long shows on the Disney service."

00:02:31.730 --> 00:02:36.200
Disney+ is the forthcoming streaming service
home to a number of Marvel superhero series

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:39.840
including Loki, WandaVision, and Falcon and
Winter Soldier.

00:02:39.840 --> 00:02:44.280
Additionally, Wardell alleged that the Black
Knight has been a hot topic of conversation

00:02:44.290 --> 00:02:45.470
at Marvel Studios.

00:02:45.470 --> 00:02:49.400
The character has flip-flopped between being
a superhero and a supervillain as several

00:02:49.400 --> 00:02:51.280
different people have brandished the moniker.

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:52.740
According to Wardell's tweet:

00:02:52.740 --> 00:02:56.240
"The Black Knight has been discussed quite
a bit over at Marvel Studios.

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.960
They see the character as a potential New
Avenger and capable of holding his own solo

00:03:00.960 --> 00:03:02.320
film, and possibly a trilogy."

00:03:02.320 --> 00:03:06.100
Wardell's final tweet on the account teased
a handful of returning villains:

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:11.300
"... Marvel still has big plans for Zemo,
Ghost, Justin Hammer, General Ross, and the

00:03:11.310 --> 00:03:12.310
[Abomination].

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:15.710
The Leader is being discussed to return as
the main villain of Thunderbolts, which is

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:17.170
being planned as a trilogy."

00:03:17.170 --> 00:03:21.880
The Leader, whose real name is Dr. Samuel
Sterns, has already appeared in the MCU: Tim

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:25.240
Blake Nelson portrayed Sterns in 2008's The
Incredible Hulk.

00:03:25.240 --> 00:03:30.290
In that flick, Sterns transformed Emil Blonsky
into the Abomination using super-soldier serum

00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:31.840
and some of Bruce Banner's blood.

00:03:31.840 --> 00:03:36.080
When the Abomination attacks Sterns, some
of Banner's blood drips into an open cut on

00:03:36.100 --> 00:03:39.600
Sterns' forehead, thus triggering his metamorphosis
into the Leader.

00:03:39.600 --> 00:03:43.980
Considering his past foundations in the MCU,
it seems plausible that the villain could

00:03:43.980 --> 00:03:46.600
rise to lead an ensemble trilogy down the
line.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:53.540
"That was the most extraordinary thing I have
seen in my entire life."

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:58.560
Given how spot-on Wardell's tweets about Avengers:
Endgame were, it's tempting to take everything

00:03:58.560 --> 00:04:02.060
he's said about the future of Marvel as 100-percent
factual.

00:04:02.060 --> 00:04:06.459
Certain elements, like Marvel planning something
major for Black Knight and the studio developing

00:04:06.460 --> 00:04:09.120
a Thunderbolts movie, seem more plausible
than others.

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:13.580
Actress Hannah John-Kamen, who played Ghost
in Ant-Man and the Wasp, once noted that she'd

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.700
love to reprise her villainous role for a
movie about the Thunderbolts.

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:19.620
She told ScreenRant in June 2018,

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:37.200
Years before that, Guardians of the Galaxy
director James Gunn shared that he told Kevin

00:04:37.200 --> 00:04:39.700
Feige he really wanted to make a Thunderbolts
movie.

00:04:39.700 --> 00:04:44.380
Maybe after Guardians of the Galaxy Vol. 3
gets out in theaters, Gunn will take on Thunderbolts

00:04:44.380 --> 00:04:45.600
as his next feature.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.180
Regarding the possibility of a Black Knight
movie, MCU Cosmic founder and editor-in-chief

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:55.180
Jeremy Conrad relayed in December 2018, not
long after Wardell shared his tweets, that

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:57.810
Marvel knows what it wants to do with the
character.

00:04:57.810 --> 00:05:01.960
Conrad, a reliable source for Marvel movie
news, tweeted at the time:

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:05.449
"There's been some hinting and talk about
Black Knight recently.

00:05:05.449 --> 00:05:08.919
Apparently Marvel does have a plan for him
in the MCU, and they already know how he'll

00:05:08.919 --> 00:05:09.919
be introduced."

00:05:09.919 --> 00:05:14.830
Still, as fun as it would be to believe Wardell's
tweets as truthful and based on insider information

00:05:14.830 --> 00:05:19.639
he obtained from Marvel brass, it's best to
take these "leaks" for what they are: unfounded

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.900
details posted by someone whose real identity
is a mystery.

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:27.540
Feige already confirmed that Marvel will announce
the first few years of its five-year, post-Endgame

00:05:27.550 --> 00:05:32.139
plan sometime after the release of Spider-Man:
Far From Home this July, so fans won't have

00:05:32.140 --> 00:05:35.640
too much longer to wait to find out the real
truth about the studio's future.

